els rounded to $Xk, indistinguishable from zero for sub-$500 values\", \"actual\": \"\\\"Income vs Expenses\\\" chart renders non-zero bars for Aug 2026 (income $450 = 162px tall, expenses $25 = 9px tall), but the Y-axis tick labels are \\\"$0k\\\", \\\"$0k\\\", \\\"$0k\\\", \\\"$0k\\\", \\\"$1k\\\". Every gridline below the top reads $0k, so the $450 and $25 values cannot be distinguished from zero on the axis.\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
